{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "wrf_thermo",
    "description": "WRF thermodynamic identities as pure expression templates, transcribed from the inline formulas WRF's physics schemes share (e.g. phys/physics_mmm/bl_ysu.F90, module_bl_ysu.F, phys/physics_mmm/mp_wsm6.F90). Every template is a closed algebraic function of its parameters: the thermodynamic constants are passed in explicitly (bind them to lib/wrf_constants.esm names, e.g. ep_1: \"wrf.ep_1\") so a template can be applied to scalars or to shaped fields alike and never reaches into a scheme's scope. Names follow WRF: theta = potential temperature (K), exner = pi = (p/p1000mb)^(r_d/cp) the Exner function (template exner_function), qv/qc/qi = vapor / cloud-water / cloud-ice mixing ratios (kg/kg).",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": ["wrf", "thermodynamics", "expression-templates"],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Skamarock, W. C., et al. (2021). A Description of the Advanced Research WRF Model Version 4.3. NCAR Technical Note NCAR/TN-556+STR. Section 2 (prognostic variables and diagnostic relations).",
        "doi": "10.5065/1dfh-6p97"
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "temperature_from_theta": {
      "params": ["theta", "exner"],
      "description": "Absolute temperature T = theta * exner from potential temperature and the Exner function (WRF: tx = thx * pi2d).",
      "body": { "op": "*", "args": ["theta", "exner"] }
    },
    "theta_from_temperature": {
      "params": ["T", "exner"],
      "description": "Potential temperature theta = T / exner (WRF: thx = tx / pi2d).",
      "body": { "op": "/", "args": ["T", "exner"] }
    },
    "virtual_potential_temperature": {
      "params": ["theta", "qv", "ep_1"],
      "description": "Virtual potential temperature theta_v = theta (1 + ep_1 qv) with ep_1 = r_v/r_d - 1 (WRF: thvx = thx * (1 + ep1 * qvx)).",
      "body": { "op": "*", "args": ["theta", { "op": "+", "args": [1, { "op": "*", "args": ["ep_1", "qv"] }] }] }
    },
    "liquid_ice_potential_temperature": {
      "params": ["theta", "qc", "qi", "exner", "xlv", "xls", "cp"],
      "description": "Liquid-ice potential temperature theta_li = theta - (xlv qc + xls qi) / (cp exner): the potential temperature the parcel would have if all condensate evaporated/sublimated (WRF YSU: thlix = (tx - xlv qcx/cp - xls qix/cp)/pi2d).",
      "body": {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
          "theta",
          { "op": "/", "args": [
            { "op": "+", "args": [{ "op": "*", "args": ["xlv", "qc"] }, { "op": "*", "args": ["xls", "qi"] }] },
            { "op": "*", "args": ["cp", "exner"] } ] }
        ]
      }
    },
    "moist_air_density": {
      "params": ["p", "T", "qv", "r_d", "ep_1"],
      "description": "Moist air density rho = p / (r_d T (1 + ep_1 qv)) from the ideal-gas law with virtual temperature (WRF: rhox = psfcpa / (rd tx (1 + ep1 qvx))).",
      "body": {
        "op": "/",
        "args": ["p", { "op": "*", "args": ["r_d", "T", { "op": "+", "args": [1, { "op": "*", "args": ["ep_1", "qv"] }] }] }]
      }
    },
    "saturation_vapor_pressure_fpvs": {
      "params": ["T", "psat", "ttp", "xa", "xb"],
      "description": "Saturation vapor pressure from the integrated Clausius-Clapeyron equation with a latent heat linear in temperature, es = psat (ttp/T)^xa exp(xb (1 - ttp/T)), where ttp is the triple-point temperature, psat the vapor pressure at ttp, xa = -(c_vapor - c_condensate)/r_v and xb = xa + L(ttp)/(r_v ttp) (the fpvs function of WRF's WSM microphysics, phys/physics_mmm/mp_wsm6.F90; over water bind c_condensate = cliq, L = xlv, over ice cice and xls). Pure function of T; the exponents are supplied so they are computed once per model.",
      "body": {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
          "psat",
          { "op": "^", "args": [{ "op": "/", "args": ["ttp", "T"] }, "xa"] },
          { "op": "exp", "args": [{ "op": "*", "args": ["xb", { "op": "-", "args": [1, { "op": "/", "args": ["ttp", "T"] }] }] }] }
        ]
      }
    },
    "fpvs_exponent_a": {
      "params": ["c_vapor", "c_condensate", "r_v"],
      "description": "Power-law exponent of saturation_vapor_pressure_fpvs, xa = -(c_vapor - c_condensate)/r_v (WSM: xa = -dldt/rv with dldt = cvap - cliq, or cvap - cice over ice).",
      "body": { "op": "-", "args": [{ "op": "/", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["c_vapor", "c_condensate"] }, "r_v"] }] }
    },
    "fpvs_exponent_b": {
      "params": ["xa", "L", "r_v", "ttp"],
      "description": "Exponential coefficient of saturation_vapor_pressure_fpvs, xb = xa + L/(r_v ttp) with L the latent heat at the triple point (WSM: xb = xa + hvap/(rv ttp)).",
      "body": { "op": "+", "args": ["xa", { "op": "/", "args": ["L", { "op": "*", "args": ["r_v", "ttp"] }] }] }
    },
    "saturation_mixing_ratio": {
      "params": ["es", "p", "ep_2"],
      "description": "Saturation mixing ratio qsat = ep_2 es / (p - es) from the saturation vapor pressure es and the total pressure p (ep_2 = r_d/r_v).",
      "body": { "op": "/", "args": [{ "op": "*", "args": ["ep_2", "es"] }, { "op": "-", "args": ["p", "es"] }] }
    },
    "latent_heat_of_vaporization": {
      "params": ["T", "xlv", "cliq", "cpv", "t0"],
      "description": "Latent heat of vaporization linear in temperature (Kirchhoff), L(T) = xlv - (cliq - cpv)(T - t0), with xlv the value at t0 (WSM: xl = xlcal(t) = xlv0 - xlv1 (t - t0c), xlv1 = cliq - cpv).",
      "body": { "op": "-", "args": ["xlv", { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["cliq", "cpv"] }, { "op": "-", "args": ["T", "t0"] }] }] }
    },
    "moist_heat_capacity": {
      "params": ["qv", "cp", "cpv"],
      "description": "Specific heat of moist air at constant pressure per unit mass, cpm = cp (1 - qv) + cpv qv (WSM: cpmcal(q) = cpd (1 - q) + q cpv).",
      "body": { "op": "+", "args": [{ "op": "*", "args": ["cp", { "op": "-", "args": [1, "qv"] }] }, { "op": "*", "args": ["qv", "cpv"] }] }
    },
    "exner_function": {
      "params": ["p", "p0", "kappa"],
      "description": "Exner function pi = (p / p0)^kappa with kappa = r_d/cp and p0 = p1000mb, so that theta = T / pi and T = theta pi (WRF pi3d/pi2d; SLAB1D THCON = (P1000mb*0.001/PL)**ROVCP is 1/pi; sf_sfclayrev thcon). Consumers: components/land_surface/slab, components/atmospheric_dynamics/sfclayrev (both formerly carried a local copy).",
      "body": { "op": "^", "args": [{ "op": "/", "args": ["p", "p0"] }, "kappa"] }
    },
    "bolton_saturation_vapor_pressure": {
      "params": ["T", "svp1", "svp2", "svp3", "svpt0"],
      "description": "Bolton (1980) saturation vapor pressure over water, e_s = svp1 exp(svp2 (T - svpt0) / (T - svp3)), in the units of svp1 (WRF: svp1 = 0.6112 kPa, svp2 = 17.67, svp3 = 29.65 K, svpt0 = 273.15 K; SLAB1D ESG = SVP1*EXP(SVP2*(TG0-SVPT0)/(TG0-SVP3)); sf_sfclayrev e1 = svp1*exp(svp2*(tsk-svpt0)/(tsk-svp3))). Consumers: components/land_surface/slab, components/atmospheric_dynamics/sfclayrev (both formerly carried a local copy). Pair with saturation_mixing_ratio for qsat.",
      "body": { "op": "*", "args": ["svp1", { "op": "exp", "args": [{ "op": "/", "args": [{ "op": "*", "args": ["svp2", { "op": "-", "args": ["T", "svpt0"] }] }, { "op": "-", "args": ["T", "svp3"] }] }] }] }
    },
    "bolton_saturation_mixing_ratio": {
      "params": ["T", "T0", "p", "es0", "a", "b", "ep_2"],
      "description": "Saturation water-vapor mixing ratio ep_2 e_s(T)/p with the Bolton (1980) fit e_s = es0 exp(a (T - T0)/(T - b)); the p - e_s denominator of saturation_mixing_ratio is omitted, exactly as bl_ysu.F90's cloud-top branch writes rvls (which also uses two different reference temperatures T0 = 273.16 and 273.15 in successive evaluations, FORTRAN_BUGS.md N7 - hence T0 is a parameter). Consumer: components/atmospheric_dynamics/ysu (formerly a local copy). For the exact form use bolton_saturation_vapor_pressure with saturation_mixing_ratio.",
      "body": { "op": "/", "args": [{ "op": "*", "args": ["es0", { "op": "exp", "args": [{ "op": "/", "args": [{ "op": "*", "args": ["a", { "op": "-", "args": ["T", "T0"] }] }, { "op": "-", "args": ["T", "b"] }] }] }, "ep_2"] }, "p"] }
    },
    "dry_air_density": {
      "params": ["p", "T", "r_d"],
      "description": "Dry-air ideal-gas density rho = p / (r_d T) (WRF radiation schemes recompute it from p and T instead of using the model's moist rho_phy: module_ra_sw.F SWPARA RO = P/(R*T); module_ra_rrtm.F MM5ATM RO = P/(R*T)*100 with P in hPa, here p in Pa). Consumers: components/atmospheric_radiation/dudhia_sw, components/atmospheric_radiation/rrtm_lw (both formerly carried a local copy). See moist_air_density for the virtual-temperature form.",
      "body": { "op": "/", "args": ["p", { "op": "*", "args": ["r_d", "T"] }] }
    }
  }
}
